Ladybird’s previews take the shapes that Gecko’s DevTools server gives
them in its previewers (ArrayLike, MapLike, DOMNode, Error, and Object,
with the same field names), since a Firefox client is what renders them.
Like Gecko’s OBJECT_PREVIEW_MAX_ITEMS, a preview lists ten items at
most. And like Gecko, it lists contents only one level down, lowercases
the nodeName of an HTML element, and calls only native getters.

Blink and WebKit build previews in their engines too, with smaller
limits for properties: The value-mirror.cc of V8 lists five names and
100 indexes at most, and the InjectedScriptSource.js of WebKit lists
five properties and ten indexes.
